    "raw": "First, let's calculate the number of ducks Philip has. Since he has 50% more ducks than cows, and he has 20 cows, the number of ducks is:\n\\[ 20 \\times 1.5 = 30 \\text{ ducks} \\]\n\nNext, we need to find out how many pigs Philip has. The total number of ducks and cows is:\n\\[ 20 + 30 = 50 \\]\nSince Philip has as many pigs as one-fifth of the total number of ducks and cows, the number of pigs is:\n\\[ \\frac{50}{5} = 10 \\text{ pigs} \\]\n\nNow, we can find the total number of animals on Philip's farm by adding the number of cows, ducks, and pigs:\n\\[ 20 + 30 + 10 = 60 \\]\n\nThus, the total number of animals on Philip's farm is:\n\\[ 60 \\]\n\nFINAL: 60",
